        "name": "units-001.json",
        "section_json": "[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"U01\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/excalidraw/lasso/utils.ts\",\n    \"action\": \"edit\",\n    \"phase\": \"codegen\",\n    \"behaviour\": \"Extend getLassoSelectedElementIds with a boxSelectionMode parameter supporting full outline and bound-text enclosure in Wrap (\\\"contain\\\") mode while preserving existing Overlap (\\\"overlap\\\") behaviour.\",\n    \"rules\": [\n      \"1. Import getElementLineSegments and isBoundToContainer from \\\"@excalidraw/element\\\", lineSegmentIntersectionPoints from \\\"@excalidraw/math\\\", and type BoxSelectionMode from \\\"../types\\\".\",\n      \"2. Add optional boxSelectionMode?: BoxSelectionMode to getLassoSelectedElementIds input parameter, destructuring with default boxSelectionMode = \\\"contain\\\".\",\n      \"3. In getLassoSelectedElementIds loop over unlockedElements, when boxSelectionMode === \\\"contain\\\" and isBoundToContainer(element) is true, skip the element so standalone bound text never selects a partially enclosed container.\",\n      \"4. Keep the fast AABB pre-filter doBoundsIntersect(lassoBounds, elementBounds) && !intersectedElements.has(element.id) && !enclosedElements.has(element.id).\",\n      \"5. When boxSelectionMode === \\\"contain\\\", add element.id to enclosedElements if and only if enclosureTest(path, element, elementsSegments, elementsMap, \\\"contain\\\") is true AND !intersectionTest(path, element, elementsMap, elementsSegments.get(element.id)) is true; do not add anything to intersectedElements in \\\"contain\\\" mode.\",\n      \"6. When boxSelectionMode === \\\"overlap\\\", preserve exact existing behaviour: if enclosureTest(path, element, elementsSegments, elementsMap, \\\"overlap\\\") is true add element.id to enclosedElements, else if intersectionTest(path, element, elementsMap) is true add element.id to intersectedElements.\",\n      \"7. In enclosureTest(lassoPath, element, elementsSegments, elementsMap, mode = \\\"overlap\\\"): resolve segments = elementsSegments.get(element.id) ?? getElementLineSegments(element, elementsMap); if !segments || segments.length"
